organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n816,\"# Celiac Disease and Nutritional Health Community\n\nThis community focuses on the interrelated entities surrounding celiac disease, its symptoms, dietary management, and associated health conditions. Key entities include celiac disease, gastrointestinal symptoms, and nutritional aspects such as cereals and gluten-free diets, highlighting the importance of proper management to prevent malnutrition and related complications.\n\n## Celiac Disease as a central health concern\n\nCeliac disease is a chronic autoimmune disorder that significantly impacts the small intestine, leading to malabsorption of nutrients. This condition is triggered by gluten ingestion in genetically predisposed individuals, resulting in inflammation and damage to the intestinal mucosa. The necessity for a strict gluten-free diet is paramount for managing this disease and preventing further health complications. The prevalence of celiac disease in certain populations underscores its importance as a public health issue, necessitating awareness and education regarding dietary restrictions and management strategies [Data: Entities (10062); Relationships (17120, 18111)].\n\n## Nutritional implications of Edema\n\nEdema, or fluid retention, can complicate the nutritional assessment and treatment of patients, particularly in children. It may indicate underlying issues such as malnutrition or congestive heart failure, which can further complicate dietary management. In the context of celiac disease, edema can arise due to malnutrition resulting from poor nutrient absorption, highlighting the need for careful monitoring and adjustments in nutritional therapy [Data: Entities (2545); Relationships (10149)].\n\n## Gastrointestinal Symptoms as key indicators\n\nGastrointestinal symptoms, such as diarrhea and bloating, are common manifestations of celiac disease and can significantly impair nutritional health. These symptoms often lead to malabsorption, which can exacerbate nutritional deficiencies. Understanding the relationship between these symptoms and celiac disease is crucial for effective diagnosis and management, as they are often the first indicators prompting further investigation into the condition [Data: Entities (1712); Relationships (4208, 7321)].\n\n## The role of Cereals in dietary management\n\nCereals are a staple in many diets, providing essential nutrients; however, they can also be a source of gluten, which is harmful to individuals with celiac disease. The dietary management of celiac disease requires careful selection of cereals that are gluten-free to prevent adverse reactions. This highlights the importance of educating patients about safe food choices and the nutritional value of gluten-free alternatives [Data: Entities (9251); Relationships (17532)].\n\n## Associated health risks with Celiac Disease\n\nCeliac disease is associated with various health risks, including malnutrition, osteoporosis, and certain autoimmune conditions. The malabsorption of nutrients can lead to deficiencies in vitamins and minerals, which may result in complications such as anemia and weakened bone health. Additionally, individuals with celiac disease are at a higher risk for developing other autoimmune disorders, necessitating comprehensive management strategies to address these interconnected health issues [Data: Entities (10434, 10441); Relationships (11011, 3604)].\n\n## Importance of a Gluten-Free Diet\n\nA gluten-free diet is essential for individuals diagnosed with celiac disease, as it helps alleviate symptoms and prevent intestinal damage. This dietary restriction is critical for managing the condition and improving the quality of life for affected individuals. The adherence to a gluten-free diet can also mitigate the risk of associated complications, making it a cornerstone of effective celiac disease management [Data: Entities (10427, 10412); Relationships (18126, 18120)].\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n13364,COMPLICACIONES POSTOPERATORIAS,\"Las complicaciones postoperatorias son efectos adversos que pueden surgir después de la cirugía, y su incidencia es especialmente alta en pacientes con cáncer, como aquellos con cáncer de páncreas y otros cánceres gastrointestinales. Estas complicaciones pueden ser más frecuentes debido a factores como la malnutrición y la pérdida de masa muscular, que son comunes en este grupo de pacientes. Para mitigar estos problemas, se busca implementar un tratamiento nutricional adecuado, lo que puede ayudar a reducir la aparición de complicaciones postoperatorias en estos individuos vulnerables.\",4\r\n9752,EMBUTIDOS,\"EMBUTIDOS are processed meats that are generally advised to be limited in children's diets due to various health concerns. These meats can sometimes contain lactose and may also include gluten, which necessitates caution for individuals with celiac disease, depending on the manufacturer's information. EMBUTIDOS typically have a high sodium content and are discouraged in diets that require gluten control, as they may contain gluten. Nutritionally, they provide 2.4 mg of iron per 100 grams, but their high fat content raises concerns, despite having an acceptable phosphorus ratio. Overall, dietary guidelines recommend that processed meats like EMBUTIDOS should be consumed occasionally and in moderation, and they are not permitted in modified diets.\",8\r\n8311,DESAYUNO,\"Desayuno refers to breakfast, the first meal of the day, which is essential for providing the necessary energy and nutrients to start the day. This meal can include a variety of specific items tailored for dietary management and restrictions, making it suitable for patients with particular health needs. Common components of a traditional desayuno may include leche (milk), pan (bread), and mermelada (jam), as well as other foods such as dairy products, cereals, and fruit. These items are important for meeting nutritional requirements and ensuring a balanced diet.\",6\r\n2247,MALABSORCIÓN,\"MALABSORCIÓN is a medical condition characterized by the impaired absorption of nutrients from the gastrointestinal tract. This condition can lead to malnutrition and is commonly observed in individuals with various underlying health issues, including inflammatory bowel disease (EII), celiac disease, pancreatic disorders, and liver disease. \n\nPatients with MALABSORCIÓN may experience difficulties in absorbing essential nutrients, which can necessitate dietary adjustments to ensure proper nutrient intake. The condition can also arise as a result of certain medical treatments, such as chemotherapy with cyclophosphamide and radiation therapy, which may further compromise nutritional status. \n\nIn individuals with celiac disease, for instance, the small intestine's inability to absorb nutrients adequately is a significant concern. Similarly, patients with cancer may face challenges related to nutrient absorption, impacting their overall health and recovery. Additionally, medications can influence nutrient absorption, potentially leading to complications such as hypophosphatemia.\n\nOverall, MALABSORCIÓN is a complex condition that requires careful management and dietary planning to address the specific needs of affected individuals.\",17\r\n10473,DIETA CONTROLADA EN GLUTEN,\"The \"\"DIETA CONTROLADA EN GLUTEN\"\" is a dietary regimen that excludes foods containing gluten. This diet is primarily recommended for individuals with celiac disease, a condition that necessitates strict avoidance of gluten to prevent adverse health effects. It is utilized mainly by those diagnosed with this condition to manage their symptoms and maintain overall health.\",16\r\n10074,HIPOALBUMINEMIA,\"Hipoalbuminemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of albumin in the blood. This condition can arise in various clinical contexts, including patients with inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatitis, celiac disease, and renal insufficiency. Hipoalbuminemia is often associated with poor nutritional status, which can lead to worse outcomes in surgical patients and indicate malnutrition and absorption issues in those with celiac disease. \n\nThe low levels of albumin can significantly affect drug metabolism and efficacy, as well as the measurement of calcium in the blood. Additionally, hipoalbuminemia decreases the oncotic pressure of plasma, contributing to fluid accumulation, particularly in cases of liver cirrhosis. Overall, hipoalbuminemia is a critical condition that reflects underlying health issues and can have serious implications for patient management and treatment outcomes.\",10\r\n1487,PAN,\"PAN refers to bread and baked goods, which are included in various meals throughout the diet plan. It is an essential ingredient in Salmorejo, contributing to the soup's texture. While bread is permitted in modified diets, it may pose risks if it is hard or crusty. Additionally, individuals with phenylketonuria should consume bread with caution, as it may contain phenylalanine. Overall, PAN encompasses a variety of bread types that can be part of a diet, but careful consideration is necessary regarding their texture and potential dietary restrictions.\",4\r\n10056,ANA M. GÓMEZ PÉREZ,\"Ana M. Gómez Pérez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition at Hospital Quirón-salud in Málaga. She is a medical professional who focuses on nutritional support for celiac disease and gluten-controlled diets, demonstrating her expertise in managing dietary needs related to these conditions.\",3\r\n10057,ROSARIO FERNÁNDEZ GARCÍA-SALAZAR,\"Dr. Rosario Fernández García-Salazar is a medical professional specializing in Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition at Hospital Quirón-salud in Málaga. She is particularly involved in providing nutritional support for celiac disease and managing gluten-controlled diets, demonstrating her expertise in addressing dietary needs related to these conditions.\",3\r\n768,HELADOS,\"HELADOS are frozen dairy products commonly known as ice creams. They are included in food frequency questionnaires and can contain gluten, which necessitates caution for individuals with celiac disease. Typically, HELADOS are made using stabilizers and emulsifiers to achieve a creamy texture, enhancing their overall quality and mouthfeel.\",3\r\n10435,DERMATITIS HERPETIFORME,\"Dermatitis herpetiforme es una erupción cutánea que se asocia con la enfermedad celíaca. Esta condición se manifiesta a través de lesiones vesículo-papulosas y pruriginosas, afectando de manera simétrica las extremidades y la región glútea.\",2\r\n12267,COBALAMINA,\"Cobalamin, also known as vitamin B12, is a crucial nutrient that can be malabsorbed in patients with pancreatic conditions, leading to deficiencies.\",2\r\n7928,HORTALIZAS,\"Las hortalizas son productos frescos que se comercializan sin envasar y deben cumplir con la normativa de etiquetado. Se consideran vegetales que deben ser consumidos en porciones diarias, y se recomienda evitar las hortalizas congeladas que contengan cremas o bechamel.\",2\r\n2245,HIPERSECRECIÓN ÁCIDA,Acid hypersecretion is an increase in gastric acid secretion that contributes to malabsorption.,1\r\n9706,MALDIGESTIÓN,\"Maldigestión is the inadequate digestion of food, which can lead to symptoms such as bloating and discomfort.\",1\r\n2246,RESECCIÓN INTESTINAL,\"Intestinal resection is a surgical procedure that removes a portion of the intestine, which can lead to malabsorption issues.\",1\r\n10500,ACEITE FRITO,El aceite que se ha empleado para freír un producto que contenga gluten es un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten.,1\r\n10496,CARNES EN CONSERVA,\"Las carnes en conserva son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten, ya que pueden contener gluten.\",1\r\n10499,CONSERVAS DE PESCADO,Las conservas de pescado en salsa o con tomate son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten.,1\r\n10501,PATATAS FRITAS,,1\r\n10494,PATATAS RELLENAS,Las patatas rellenas de ketchup y/o mostaza son un alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten.,1\r\n10497,PESCADOS REBOZADOS,\"Los pescados rebozados son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten, ya que contienen gluten.\",1\r\n10498,SUCEDÁNEOS DE MARISCO,\"Los sucedáneos de marisco son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten, ya que pueden contener gluten.\",1\r\n11529,CARNE FRESCA,\"Fresh meat has a phosphorus ratio below 16 mg/g, with recommendations for white meat like chicken and turkey.\",1\r\n11530,JAMONES,Ham is recommended due to lower fat content and an acceptable phosphorus ratio between 3.64 and 12.57 mg/g.,1\r\n15371,\"NUTRICIÓN(\"\"ENTITY\"\"\",,1\r\n8277,FRUTA,\"FRUTA refers to a variety of fruits that are included in dietary plans, specifically noted to exclude bananas. These fruits serve as a dessert option within the diet plan and are often incorporated into meals and snacks due to their nutritional benefits and natural sweetness.\",1\r\n10402,HOSPITAL QUIRÓN-SALUD,\"Hospital Quirón-salud is a clinical hospital specializing in endocrinology and clinical nutrition located in Málaga, Spain.\",2\r\n763,EMULSIFICANTE,\"El emulsificante es un compuesto que ayuda a mezclar ingredientes que normalmente no se combinarían, como el agua y el aceite, en productos alimentarios.\",1\r\n14046,SÍNDROME DE HEINER,\"El síndrome de Heiner es una enfermedad rara que causa hemosiderosis pulmonar, típicamente ocasionada por proteínas de la leche de vaca.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n2776,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,COMPLICACIONES POSTOPERATORIAS,La nutrición enteral puede ayudar a disminuir la incidencia de complicaciones postoperatorias en pacientes con cáncer gástrico,339\r\n17945,EMBUTIDOS,NUTRICIÓN PEDIÁTRICA,Processed meats should be consumed occasionally and in moderation according to dietary guidelines,170\r\n17076,DESAYUNO,NUTRICIÓN PEDIÁTRICA,Desayuno is a critical meal outlined in the NUTRICIÓN PEDIÁTRICA guidelines for children's nutrition,168\r\n7290,MALNUTRICIÓN,MALABSORCIÓN,La malabsorción puede causar malnutrición al impedir que el cuerpo absorba los nutrientes necesarios,121\r\n9419,MALABSORCIÓN,ENFERMEDAD CELIACA,\"MALABSORCIÓN y ENFERMEDAD CELIACA están interrelacionadas, ya que la malabsorción es una complicación común de la enfermedad celíaca. Esta condición resulta en deficiencias nutricionales, lo que indica que la malabsorción e